# Harness project

This repo is a file agent: an OpenAI-compatible chat loop, tools confined to one workspace, and a JSONL trace in that workspace's `session.log`.

- `src/harnh3x/config.py` holds `PROVIDER`, `API_KEY`, `API_URL`, `MAX_TOKENS`, `CONTEXT_LIMIT`, `MODEL`, `MAX_TURNS`, `COMPACT_AT`, `MAX_TOOL_RESULT`, the fetch/search/feed limits, `SHELL_TIMEOUT` and `SHELL_MAX_TIMEOUT`, the file listing and search caps, `PDF_MAX_PAGES`, `PREVIEW_ROWS`, `MEMORY_FILE`, `PLAN_FILE`, `TRANSCRIPT_FILE`, `WIKIPEDIA_LANG`, and `BASE_DIR` (default `~/.harnh3x`, expanded when it is absolute or starts with `~`). Sessions live in `BASE_DIR/workspaces`. `MEMORY_FILE` is `BASE_DIR/memory.md`, shared across sessions. `~/.config/harnh3x/harnh3x.yaml` (or `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/harnh3x/harnh3x.yaml`) is YAML and can set the API key, API URL, and those tunables except `MEMORY_FILE`, `PLAN_FILE`, and `TRANSCRIPT_FILE`. A non-empty process environment variable overrides the file for those scalars, and a working-directory `.env` fills variables that are not already set. `HARNH3X_CONFIG` selects another file; an empty value skips it. `mcp` is a mapping of stdio servers (`command`, `args`, `env`, `timeout`, `description`, `include`, `exclude`). Environment variables do not override `mcp`. If `harnh3x.conf` exists and `harnh3x.yaml` does not, startup exits and names both files. `MCP_SERVERS` holds the validated servers. `provider` is `openai` (default) or `anthropic`. Startup exits when `api_key` is unset, and when `api_url` is unset for `openai`. For `anthropic`, the key is `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` when that variable is set, otherwise `api_key`; `OPENAI_API_KEY` does not override it. `api_url` defaults to `https://api.anthropic.com`. `max_tokens` defaults to 8192. `context_limit` is optional; Claude compaction uses 200000 when it is unset. `--yolo` stays a launch flag.
- `src/harnh3x/anthropic_api.py` translates the stored transcript to the Anthropic Messages API and maps the stream back into the same assistant message. `get_client()` returns that client when `provider` is `anthropic`.
- `src/harnh3x/prompt.py` builds the system prompt: date and OS, a one-line workspace listing, the saved memory keys, the prompt contract, and the skill menu. It accepts `now` for tests, `yolo` to add the unsandboxed-session sentence, `project` to name a granted folder and point code changes there, `rules` for that folder's Cursor rules, and `coding` to replace the assistant contract with a coding-agent prompt.
- `src/harnh3x/rules.py` reads `<project>/.cursor/rules/**/*.mdc` only in a coding session. `alwaysApply` rules go in the system prompt. `globs` may be a comma-separated line or a YAML list; a matching file tool appends that rule once. A symlink that resolves outside the project is skipped. A bad frontmatter block is skipped.
- `src/harnh3x/tools/` defines the tool schema and the sandbox. Each skill module exports its schemas and functions. `TOOLS` is the full domain catalog assembled from those modules.
- `src/harnh3x/skills/` holds `SkillRegistry` plus one `SKILL.md` per skill: `file_ops`, `shell`, `python`, `coding`, `research`, `reference`, `http`, `documents`, `data`, `memory`, `tasks`, and `sql-injection`. A skill may live in a category subdirectory (`skills/<category>/<name>/SKILL.md`, any depth) and is still named by its folder. Every tool belongs to exactly one skill. The loop sends `load_skill`, `unload_skill`, and schemas for loaded skills only; several skills can be loaded at once. Configured MCP servers are extra skills in category `mcp`. Their tool schemas come from the server when the skill is loaded, not from `TOOLS`. `src/harnh3x/mcp/` is the stdio client. A server named `caido` also gets `src/harnh3x/mcp/guides/caido.md`. The child is not Seatbelt-sandboxed. `unload_skill` drops its schemas and leaves the process up. `reset()`, `resume()`, and process exit close it. An MCP skill is omitted when an `http` or `https` URL in its `env` is not accepting connections. A handshake that cannot finish removes that skill from the menu.
- `src/harnh3x/agent.py` owns `Session` and `run`. `Session.reset()` starts a new conversation in a new workspace, keeping the model, `yolo`, `project`, `coding`, and `debug`. `Session.resume()` reloads a workspace's `transcript.json`, restores `project` and `coding` from that file, replays skill loads, and refreshes the system prompt. `reset()` and `resume()` clear the set of glob rules already appended. A transcript with no `project` clears any launch grant. A transcript with no `coding`, or with `coding` false, clears a launch coding session. A non-boolean `coding` value fails resume. `coding` is stored in the transcript when the session is a coding session. `yolo` and `debug` stay launch flags and are not stored in the transcript. `reset()` and `resume()` keep `debug`.
- `src/harnh3x/cli.py` is the CLI, exposed as the `harnh3x` console script. `--project PATH` grants sandboxed read, write, and shell access to one existing directory that must not overlap the session workspace; `/` is rejected. Relative paths and the shell working directory use that folder. `--coding` requires `--project` and starts a coding session: a coding system prompt, and Cursor rules from that project. The flag is stored in `transcript.json` and restored by `/resume`. Ctrl+N keeps it. Plain output and the header print `Coding` on the line after `Project:`. `--debug` shows the system prompt once at the start of the session, and again only when that prompt changes, plus the other messages sent on each completion, in cyan panels that keep the last three lines until a click expands them. It is not stored. Ctrl+N and `/resume` keep it. Plain output and the header print `Debug` on the line after `Coding`. `--answer-only` hides those panels. The summary call is not shown. `--yolo` disables the seatbelt sandbox: read tools may open any path, shell and Python may run any program, including sudo, and HTTP tools may use any host, including localhost and private addresses. File mutation tools stay in the workspace, or in the project when one is granted. A tty session uses Textual (`src/harnh3x/tui.py`): a header whose title is Harnh3x followed by the package version, then the workspace, the project when one is set, Coding when the session is a coding session, Debug when `--debug` is set, model, and context used against the model's limit, then the transcript. In yolo mode the header’s first line is `YOLO — sandbox off` in bright yellow, and that mark stays after Ctrl+N and `/resume`. Plain stdout prints the same warning before the workspace and model. `--answer-only` stays the final answer only. The composer takes Enter to submit and Shift+Enter for a newline. Ctrl+Q and `/exit` quit. Ctrl+N starts a new session in a new workspace and refreshes the header path. Ctrl+H hides or shows every thinking box, tool box, debug box, and compaction note, including ones added while they are hidden. `/help` opens a box of commands and hotkeys that Escape closes. `/resume` opens a list of past sessions and restores that transcript. `/compact` forces a context compaction. Each model round's tool calls share a bordered box, in the order the API produced them. That box keeps the last three lines until a click expands it. Thinking and the answer update while the completion streams; each thinking box keeps the last three lines until a click expands it. While output is arriving, the transcript stays at the bottom until the user scrolls up, and scrolling back to the bottom follows again. A context compaction shows Compacting context… while the summary runs, then a Context compacted note, and the agent answer is rendered as Markdown. One-shot on a tty starts that view before the request so tokens are visible as they arrive, and waits for Enter to close when the turn included reasoning. Plain stdout writes reasoning and the answer as the tokens arrive. `/resume` reprints a finished transcript in that same order, with the collapsed thinking panel for a finished reasoning block. Piped input and `--answer-only` stay plain stdout. `--model` with no name uses the Textual list on a tty and a numbered prompt otherwise. Tests live in `tests/test_harnh3x.py`.
- Export new public symbols from `src/harnh3x/__init__.py` `__all__`.

Poetry with `package-mode = true` and a `poetry-core` build backend so pip and pipx install the `harnh3x` script. Pytest uses `pythonpath = ["src"]`. Format with Black. Do not commit `src/.env`.

A new tool, or a looser path or shell check, needs a matching test.

```python
# BAD: a second model constant next to the loop
MODEL = "other"

# GOOD: change the constant in src/harnh3x/config.py
from harnh3x.config import MODEL
```
